---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://catchment.school';
const org = {
  '@type': 'Organization',
  '@id': `${SITE}/#organization`,
  name: 'catchment.school',
  url: SITE,
  logo: `${SITE}/favicon.svg`,
  description: 'Free school catchment area checker and school statistics for England, with Welsh schools listed from the DfE register, built from Department for Education and Ofsted data.',
  areaServed: 'GB',
};
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'AboutPage',
      '@id': `${SITE}/about/#webpage`,
      url: `${SITE}/about/`,
      name: 'About catchment.school',
      description: 'Who runs catchment.school, where its data comes from and how to report a mistake.',
      inLanguage: 'en-GB',
      dateModified: '2026-10-31',
      isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'catchment.school', url: SITE },
      mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE}/#organization` },
    },
    org,
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="About catchment.school - Who Runs It and Where the Data Comes From"
  description="catchment.school is a free, independent school information site for parents. Data comes from the Department for Education and Ofsted. See sources, method and how to report a mistake."
  canonical="https://catchment.school/about/"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6 flex gap-2" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
    <span>›</span>
    <span>About</span>
  </nav>

  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">About catchment.school</h1>

    <!-- Site coverage -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-700 mb-1">26,506</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Open schools listed</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-700 mb-1">178</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Local authorities covered</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-700 mb-1">Free</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">No registration required</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="prose prose-lg">
      <h2>What is catchment.school?</h2>
      <p>
        catchment.school helps parents and carers find schools near them. It shows the published Ofsted, admissions, results and workforce figures for each school and explains how school admissions work.
        It lists 26,506 open schools in 178 local authorities, including the Welsh establishments that the Get Information About Schools register holds.
      </p>

      <h2>Is catchment.school independent?</h2>
      <p>
        catchment.school is an independent information site. It is not a school admissions service or a law firm. The site reports published government data and does not give advice on individual applications.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is free to use and is not affiliated with any school, trust or local authority. The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains how the site is funded and how it handles links to TheTutorLink.
      </p>

      <h2>Where does the data come from?</h2>
      <p>
        School details come from the
        <a href="https://get-information-about-schools.service.gov.uk" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Get Information About Schools (GIAS)</a> register,
        maintained by the
        <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-education" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Department for Education</a>.
        Inspection outcomes come from Ofsted. Admissions, results, absence, workforce, spending and special educational needs figures come from DfE statistical releases.
        Everything is used under the
        <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> lists each dataset with its publisher, release, link and download date. It also explains how distances and rankings are worked out and what the data cannot show.
      </p>

      <h2>What is a school catchment area?</h2>
      <p>
        A catchment area is the geographic zone from which a school gives priority to applications.
        Living inside it can improve the chance of a place. It does not guarantee one at an oversubscribed school.
        Catchment areas are set by local authorities and individual schools, and they can change each year.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/guides/how-school-catchment-areas-work">Read the full guide to how catchment areas work →</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Does catchment.school show catchment boundaries?</h2>
      <p>
        No. The site does not hold boundary maps. It shows the figures the DfE publishes, such as first preferences and places offered.
        School pages link to a search for the council's admissions policy. Check the policy for your year of entry, or contact your local authority, before you rely on a catchment.
      </p>

      <h2>How do I report a mistake?</h2>
      <p>
        Use the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. It says what to include and what happens to your report.
      </p>

      <h2>How to use this site</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong><a href="/postcode/">Search by postcode</a></strong> - find schools within 5 km of your home address</li>
        <li><strong><a href="/council">Browse by council</a></strong> - see all schools in your local authority</li>
        <li><strong><a href="/area">Browse by town</a></strong> - see all schools in your town</li>
        <li><strong><a href="/guides">Read the guides</a></strong> - understand admissions, catchment areas and application deadlines</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
